event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":334,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_07239f830d7d4c21016acb58d649c881978f1a066b0d3c788e","object":"response","created_at":1791711446,"completed_at":1791711459,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_07239f830d7d4c21016acb58d74f58819798f4de497a92f466","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Reviewing JSON tests**\n\nI need to make sure the retention test for JSON is checked explicitly, ensuring everything is properly escaped and matched. It's acceptable, but I'm wondering if I should add larger notes for checking. With newline conversions for CRLF in the textarea, it seems fine since JSON strings are escaped. I also have to consider that DB validation might ignore unknown malicious fields. I'm glad the default works and everything is being stored correctly, even starting with a newline!"}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy1jc8BWEsA-_ufrAnBTGUypZ9NLzwEORxCdPE8o_UDhIVUdTyNfvmwKRExvtz3HCSzQ4fwgRpshWKB7a6GA3diSqDl9Lu1C3gZqdE9uxYSMws4HQjPiU3uxWejWizzw47ANVCZvxhIxF4ETrXIQ6X2MZW2FMI73AVXAtbK_PQeD5-mQJU5CV470R5bnSci9pQatB8l7DjecStkOOje9siKl3ktDeEvqGK459oWolL9njC_i7yQSxto9E4xL7OFdVRlOvih33vVmLeVNpmy9HL8Ee8bTEJa8NyAtRZ98eWSDpyHqal-X4v3GipcrtXEXKyBdu836WtJzfhby5wJUo9mePKrXoHCXj3HbvZl4sd-AIsvi-kN2Q0jNsrAYbNO-jAad2Xs_mYTFlA8lPEQUmHz3-FmFMQWjJR3ox9eIy3DkXGSBEy2CjDn2A_J4d3JTekUhcZfqoNSyWkI6Rr0h_5TM9aj1zmdud7IDA7Re8vX0QoU1a8zlasTNsQrHgk_DNUNc8TTZXrt2HnrTtArCmRLbYigG2TEZEiY6vO8pJNlhkqMbhCGwhyK1CnEziHAywmmOwhDpsAjwAtoKKsFl0zB59GaqgiH_Z8FDxIB64T6kNiAg3d2bBOTvWktj24gzUJQNHiAPIVcM9r7eDvfNb0WT70bdLBH_mArSRiRPV7V1nnWhaTRRfFwWcO61ei9zOYgMBgVvNADbLXET0co6xc2RIB8jSulWvgVCYUK3MCLFNv8KlJKdQkh1YMpaPhDc7guE5PYa2rhRZdc37scj9ET_T9zy8lkxPtzSEA9_tFau30yAD7pYaIfa_6XpIYTG9uQNnlGXAfBhXt6I1r63xbosxSilzBOW07w1x-bIiOCjWdFUpfbwZ9deyROh66o3M2DyUymEX0iODFiviwPiu7nWYg8txxU45s1nuxX2TGdnKssTkg1V78qLHeBswbZcA4QfhqD3Jzyi8SYQiF1KFemFNttxDEuf47U1kWOzWA4SPOhv68IWuPs7wk9WY-Qi10ayzFA5YYAHHR3kxLA0T446rEtVmkXyDATVW4NAWz7SKSUUZrq4AxtQROWJJY_BvuM-sxKh-YFIgjONQUlkY3wq8OE5TvjQLNVqqhH5n5F83Zu7SRIsvb-Jjo8Aqvj0QtKUMlK_d2UbeyGG-SjAiCMNnI8p0ZJAZKjy6TQGPawK2vU2meXg-jl3f6L91Qcg0KxL-TdiSd4j5213KhJy64tkAvrHIgoXvfVtXA2CH5I6KiBq4noRtG2bmia2A31vTBOdL_ljDQBhPrV9by3IiKOpFNGkLjHtQbuLUO8VmAg6A0G4w_bylpvrcR8qMPbYBhCfA5ktBaI4XPQ-HvmwgFJq7qWgkXQGlhu1ghTBEHECML9eqlGmMP0JcXEvrF70TnoIHsI1BwWCmq4DK4VArNZfkjmyXIPeC2wMps0tIefDVuRO8_Y6UqCFXlaqWwCkbY8k31x5mkx3LB4UqLauwhaeOiNDNYGhs2I7pI1PJUhNWVswqt7uTTpZYzm_w5q798LxMjmSgbOk5SqFnozRWpl5eGzaGiQuRS-k-ivgOY2pGXFCJa1W8zbB1FNXTUa9CGf9FTZWLpfhWx2J1mTz-E45nXx2iSDc9CGhh9f_sHCjT95bORpbUi4cn2LxNgaU1NgFTNSJrHhCCZIYIKRQFQ5gdmTvWai8ks1-8mEWu8_F6obG-P0HsEyTKyn98Jluu3YWcF4O8xJP_BeXVlMauCDK27ELMFZZRKKOy2zUygUpV1M7ubzRLlH9Dk9Wrj7jOMAQpy0-uOsKnivcCufHvaX8m3aFSgH1WtLQJzN7W0QLm-vO1zfGZ2uAOoAEMQJ5SR253BSYaih3cmwbKktdy8-eQmybgBlMVgl-SDEuIDlL3oR